{
  "an10.95:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 10.95 ",
  "an10.95:0.2": "10. With Upāli ",
  "an10.95:0.3": "With Uttiya ",
  "an10.95:1.1": "Then the wanderer Uttiya went up to the Buddha, and exchanged greetings with him. ",
  "an10.95:1.2": "When the greetings and polite conversation were over, he sat down to one side and said to the Buddha, ",
  "an10.95:1.3": "“Worthy Gotama, is this right: ‘The cosmos is eternal. This is the only truth, anything else is futile’?” ",
  "an10.95:1.4": "“This has not been declared by me, Uttiya.” ",
  "an10.95:1.5": "",
  "an10.95:2.1": "“Then is this right: ‘The cosmos is not eternal. This is the only truth, anything else is futile’?” ",
  "an10.95:2.2": "“This has not been declared by me, Uttiya.” ",
  "an10.95:2.3": "",
  "an10.95:3.1": "“Then is this right: ‘The cosmos is finite …’ … ",
  "an10.95:3.2": "‘The cosmos is infinite …’ … ",
  "an10.95:3.3": "‘The soul and the body are one and the same …’ … ",
  "an10.95:3.4": "‘The soul is one thing, the body another …’ … ",
  "an10.95:3.5": "‘A realized one still exists after death …’ … ",
  "an10.95:3.6": "‘A realized one no longer exists after death …’ … ",
  "an10.95:3.7": "‘A realized one both still exists and no longer exists after death …’ … ",
  "an10.95:3.8": "‘A realized one neither still exists nor no longer exists after death. This is the only truth, anything else is futile’?” ",
  "an10.95:3.9": "“This has not been declared by me